{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"All 16 workloads are correct. The large-shape slowdown is isolated to atomic contention in `grad_weight`, so I’m replacing that reducer with a two-stage deterministic partial sum: each tile writes a private column partial, then one contiguous reduction per hidden feature finishes it. This removes millions of contended atomics while adding only a small temporary buffer."}}
