{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"The two-stage reducer is already about 4× faster than the reference, but it still rereads 8 GB of input on the largest workload. With two attempts left, I’m testing a genuinely fused design: each program processes a small row group, emits both BF16 gradients, and accumulates private `grad_weight` partials from the same loads. A coalesced hierarchy then reduces those partials. Row-group size will scale with workload size to preserve occupancy on the tiny cases."}}
